dable (unescaped) form; **in the file they carry one level of JSON escaping** (`\\\\b`, `\\\\d`, \u2026). Byte-exact quoting must be taken from `master_data_classifiers/ruleset.json`.\n\n### A1. `CLS-PII-CC-001` \u2014 Credit Card Number\n```json\n{{\n  \"classifier_id\": \"CLS-PII-CC-001\",\n  \"category\": \"PII.FINANCIAL.CREDIT_CARD\",\n  \"type\": \"regex\",\n  \"pattern\": \"\\\\b(?:4\\\\d{{3}}|5[1-5]\\\\d{{2}}|6011|3[47]\\\\d{{2}})[- ]?\\\\d{{4}}[- ]?\\\\d{{4}}[- ]?\\\\d{{4}}\\\\b|\\\\b\\\\d{{4}}-\\\\d{{4}}-\\\\d{{4}}-\\\\d{{4}}\\\\b\",\n  \"confidence_threshold\": 0.95,\n  \"priority\": 1,\n  \"mask_token\": \"[CREDIT_CARD]\",\n  \"validators\": \"ABSENT\",\n  \"match_strategy\": \"ABSENT\"\n}}\n```\n\n### A2. `CLS-PII-IBAN-001` \u2014 Bank Account (IBAN)\n```json\n{{\n  \"classifier_id\": \"CLS-PII-IBAN-001\",\n  \"category\": \"PII.FINANCIAL.BANK_ACCOUNT\",\n  \"type\": \"regex\",\n  \"pattern\": \"\\\\b[A-Z]{{2}}\\\\d{{2}}(?:\\\\s?[A-Z0-9]{{4}}){{3,7}}\\\\b\",\n  \"confidence_threshold\": 0.90,\n  \"priority\": 2,\n  \"mask_token\": \"[BANK_ACCOUNT]\",\n  \"validators\": \"ABSENT\",\n  \"match_strategy\": \"ABSENT\"\n}}\n```\nNote: named \"IBAN\" but bound to `PII.FINANCIAL.BANK_ACCOUNT` / `[BANK_ACCOUNT]`; the enum member `PII.FINANCIAL.IBAN` is targeted by **no** classifier.\n\n### A3. `CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001` \u2014 Residential / Work Street Address\n```json\n{{\n  \"classifier_id\": \"CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001\",\n  \"category\": \"PII.LOCATION.STREET_ADDRESS\",\n  \"type\": \"regex\",\n  \"pattern\": \"\\\\b\\\\d{{1,5}}\\\\s+[A-Za-z0-9\\\\s.,]+(?:Terrace|Street|St|Avenue|Ave|Road|Rd|Boulevard|Blvd|Way|Lane|Ln|Drive|Dr)(?:[A-Za-z0-9\\\\s.,#]+)?(?:,\\\\s+[A-Za-z\\\\s]+,\\\\s+[A-Z]{{2}}\\\\s+\\\\d{{5}}(?:-\\\\d{{4}})?)?\\\\b\",\n  \"confidence_threshold\": 0.85,\n  \"priority\": 4,\n  \"mask_token\": \"[STREET_ADDRESS]\",\n  \"validators\": \"ABSENT\",\n  \"match_strategy\": \"ABSENT\"\n}}\n```\n\n### A4. `CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001` \u2014 Medical Case Ref / Patient Member ID\n```json\n{{\n  \"classifier_id\": \"CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001\",\n  \"category\": \"PHI.MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER\",\n  \"type\": \"regex\",\n  \"pattern\": \"\\\\b(?:MC|MEM|PAT|REC)-[A-Za-z0-9-]{{4,15}}\\\\b\",\n  \"confidence_threshold\": 0.90,\n  \"priority\": 2,\n  \"mask_token\": \"[MEDICAL_ID]\",\n  \"validators\": \"ABSENT\",\n  \"match_strategy\": \"ABSENT\"\n}}\n```\nNote: `category` has **no type suffix**, so it binds to neither `PATIENT_ID` nor `MEDICAL_CASE_REF`.\n\n### A5. Current category enum trees (verbatim)\n```\nPII\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 PERSON_NAME         (no types array \u2014 leaf)\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 IDENTIFIER          types: [\"SSN\", \"NATIONAL_ID\", \"PASSPORT\", \"DRIVERS_LICENSE\"]\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 CONTACT             types: [\"EMAIL\", \"PHONE_NUMBER\"]\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 LOCATION            types: [\"STREET_ADDRESS\", \"IP_ADDRESS\"]\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 FINANCIAL           types: [\"CREDIT_CARD\", \"BANK_ACCOUNT\", \"IBAN\", \"CVV\"]\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 DEMOGRAPHIC         types: [\"DATE_OF_BIRTH\"]\n\nPHI\n\u251c\u2500\u2500 MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER  types: [\"PATIENT_ID\", \"MEDICAL_CASE_REF\"]\n\u2514\u2500\u2500 HEALTH_DATA         types: [\"ALLERGY\", \"CONDITION\", \"PRESCRIPTION\", \"CLINICAL_NOTE\"]\n```\nrev-001 inventory: **13 classifiers**; history has 1 entry (`CREATE_INITIAL_PINNED_REVISION`, added 13, modified 0, removed 0); `pending_admin_review: []`.\n\n---\n\n## (B) EVIDENCE OF DEFECTS \u2014 measured, not asserted\n\nAll results below were produced by executing the patterns against the exact evidence strings.\n\n### B1. `CLS-PII-CC-001` \u2014 0 matches on `test_file.pdf` (3 occurrences of the card)\n**Root cause confirmed: the separator class `[- ]?` admits exactly one character, and only hyphen or space \u2014 never a newline, and never two whitespace chars.**\n\n| Test input | rev-001 pattern | Corrected pattern |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Visa 4532-\\n8910-4321-9081` | **no match** | match `[5,25]` |\n| `4532-8910-4321-9081` | match `[0,19]` | match `[0,19]` |\n| `4532-\\n8910-\\n4321-9081` | **no match** | match `[0,21]` |\n| `4532  8910  4321  9081` (double spaces) | **no match** | match |\n| `4532-\\n\\n8910-4321-9081` (blank line) | no match | **no match** (guard holds) |\n| `order 1234\\n5678\\n9012` (12 digits) | no match | no match |\n| `ref 2026\\n1016` (date-like) | no match | no match |\n| `3782 822463 10005` (Amex 4-6-5, 15 digit) | no match | **no match \u2014 out of scope, see risk R1** |\n\n**Corrected separator class requirement:** must accept `hyphen`, spaces/tabs (runs of any length), and **at most one newline** per separator, but must **not** allow a blank line (which would let a match bridge two unrelated paragraphs).\n\n**Corrected pattern (validated):**\n```json\n\"pattern\": \"\\\\b(?:\\\\d{{4}}(?:[ \\\\t\\\\-]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t\\\\-]*)){{3}}\\\\d{{4}}\\\\b\"\n```\nHuman-readable: `\\b(?:\\d{{4}}(?:[ \\t\\-]*\\n?[ \\t\\-]*)){{3}}\\d{{4}}\\b`\n\n**Luhn post-validator (new `validators` block) \u2014 and the conflict:**\n```\nluhn(digits):\n  digits = [int(c) for c in re.sub(r'\\D','',match)]\n  return (sum(digits[-1::-2]) + sum(sum(divmod(2*d,10)) for d in digits[-2::-2])) % 10 == 0\n```\n- `4111111111111111` \u2192 **pass** (digit-sum 30)\n- `4012888888881881` \u2192 **pass** (digit-sum 90)\n- `4532891043219081` (**the card actually present in `test_file.pdf`**) \u2192 **FAIL** (digit-sum 72)\n\n**Therefore a hard Luhn gate is unsafe on the current corpus.** Proposed **two-tier soft-fail** design (Admin must select Option 1 or 2):\n\n```json\n\"validators\": [\n  {{ \"id\": \"luhn_mod10\", \"type\": \"checksum\", \"algorithm\": \"LUHN\",\n    \"on_pass\": {{ \"confidence\": 0.99, \"status\": \"LUHN_PASS\" }},\n    \"on_fail\": {{ \"confidence\": 0.86, \"status\": \"LUHN_FAIL\", \"emit_metadata\": true }} }}\n],\n\"confidence_threshold\": 0.85\n```\n- **Option 1 (recommended):** `confidence_threshold: 0.85`, base confidence 0.88, Luhn-pass 0.99, Luhn-fail 0.86 \u2192 the document's card is detected **and** flagged `validator_status: LUHN_FAIL` for reviewer attention.\n- **Option 2 (strict precision):** `confidence_threshold: 0.95`, Luhn-fail suppressed \u2192 **the defect is NOT fixed for `test_file.pdf`**; would require the Human Admin to accept a known false negative.\n\n### B2. `CLS-PII-IBAN-001` \u2014 truncation of the final 2-char group\n**Root cause confirmed: `(?:\\s?[A-Z0-9]{{4}}){{3,7}}` forces every group to be exactly 4 chars, so a short final group can never be captured.**\n\n| Test input | rev-001 pattern | Corrected pattern |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Account: US39 OBAK 0123 4567 8901 23 (ref)` | match span **(9,33)** = `US39 OBAK 0123 4567 8901` \u2014 ends at 33, leaving ` 23` behind | match span **(9,36)** = `US39 OBAK 0123 4567 8901 23` |\n| `US39\\nOBAK 0123 4567 8901 23` | no match (`\\s?`+`{{4}}` interaction) | match `[0,27]` |\n| space-only variant on the newline input | no match | \u2014 (proves the newline must be admitted) |\n| `US39\\n\\nOBAK 0123` | no match | **no match** (blank-line guard) |\n| `The US39 code` / `AB12` | no match | no match |\n\nThis reproduces the reported `[439,463]` truncation exactly (relative span 9\u219233, length 24; in the document `[439,463]`).\n\n**Corrected pattern (validated), variable-length final group + bounded newline:**\n```json\n\"pattern\": \"\\\\b[A-Z]{{2}}\\\\d{{2}}(?:[ \\\\t]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t]*[A-Z0-9]{{4}}){{1,7}}(?:[ \\\\t]*\\\\n?[ \\\\t]*[A-Z0-9]{{1,3}})?\\\\b\"\n```\nHuman-readable: `\\b[A-Z]{{2}}\\d{{2}}(?:[ \\t]*\\n?[ \\t]*[A-Z0-9]{{4}}){{1,7}}(?:[ \\t]*\\n?[ \\t]*[A-Z0-9]{{1,3}})?\\b`\nAdd post-filter `strip_separators` \u2192 assert cleaned alnum length in **10..34** (IBAN max) before emitting.\n\n**Does `'US39' + NEWLINE + 'OBAK'` become detectable? YES** under the corrected pattern \u2014 **only because** the separator is `[ \\t]*\\n?[ \\t]*` rather than `[ ]?` (the space-only variant returns **no match**). This is a direct dependency of the fix: do **not** narrow the corrected separator to a single space.\n\n### B3. `CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001` \u2014 over-extension swallowing `\\nSocial Security Number`\n**Root cause confirmed: the trailing optional class `[A-Za-z0-9\\s.,#]+` contains `\\s`, so it consumes newlines, and it contains digits, so it consumes the start of the SSN line.**\n\n| Test input | rev-001 pattern | Corrected pattern |\n|---|---|---|\n| `1200 Market Street Suite 400\\nSocial Security Number 123-45-6789` | span **(0,55)**, captured `'1200 Market Street Suite 400\\nSocial Security Number 123'` \u2014 **crosses the newline into the label and into the SSN digits** | span **(0,28)** = `'1200 Market Street Suite 400'`, stops **before** the newline |\n| `742 Evergreen Terrace, Springfield, IL 62704\\nPhone: 555-0100` | \u2014 | `'742 Evergreen Terrace, Springfield, IL 62704'` (ZIP retained, stops at newline) |\n| `500 West 5th Ave\\nNew York` | \u2014 | `'500 West 5th Ave'` |\n| `No address here at all` | \u2014 | no match |\n\n**Corrected boundary rule:** the address body (number, street tokens, street-type suffix, secondary unit) may use **`[ \\t]` only \u2014 never `\\s`**, and may contain no more than 6 street tokens; the semantic address terminates at the last address token before any newline, so a `\\n` + label boundary can never be entered. Plus the `Suite|Ste|Unit|Apt|Bldg|Floor|Fl` secondary-unit group and the `, City, ST ZIP(+4)` group become explicit optional groups with the **same** `[ \\t]`-only discipline.\n\n**Corrected pattern (validated):**\n```json\n\"pattern\": \"\\\\b\\\\d{{1,5}}[ \\\\t]+(?:[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9.\\\\-#]*[ \\\\t]+){{0,6}}(?:Terrace|Street|St|Avenue|Ave|Road|Rd|Boulevard|Blvd|Way|Lane|Ln|Drive|Dr)\\\\b(?:[ \\\\t]*,[ \\\\t]*(?:Suite|Ste|Unit|Apt|Bldg|Floor|Fl)[ \\\\t]*#?[0-9A-Za-z-]+|[ \\\\t]+(?:Suite|Ste|Unit|Apt|Bldg|Floor|Fl)[ \\\\t]*#?[0-9A-Za-z-]+)?(?:,[ \\\\t]+[A-Za-z .]+,[ \\\\t]+[A-Z]{{2}}[ \\\\t]+\\\\d{{5}}(?:-\\\\d{{4}})?)?\"\n```\nAdd post-filter `truncate_at_newline`: if a match still contains `\\n` (defensive), trim to the last `[ \\t]`-delimited token before it and re-check it ends on an address token.\n\n### B4. `CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001` \u2014 zero matches for `HI-902849102-B`\n**Confirmed.** `\\b(?:MC|MEM|PAT|REC)-[A-Za-z0-9-]{{4,15}}\\b` returns **no match** against `Member ID: HI-902849102-B on file`. The anchor set `MC|MEM|PAT|REC` does not include `HI`, and the trailing `\\b` would not accommodate the `-B` suffix pattern as a distinct segment. The correct fix is **not** to add `HI` to `MED-ID` (that would conflate a case ref with an insurance member ID) but to add a distinct classifier \u2014 see (C2). Additionally the existing classifier's body `[A-Za-z0-9-]{{4,15}}` is too loose (accepts `REC-1234`), so a MED-ID tightening is proposed separately in (B5).\n\n### B5. Optional MED-ID tightening (recommended, low risk)\n`\"pattern\": \"\\\\b(?:MC|MEM|PAT|REC)-\\\\d{{6,12}}(?:-[A-Z0-9]{{1,2}})?\\\\b\"` \u2014 keeps existing true positives (`REC-2026-0042` style needs the hyphen branch, so Admin should confirm the corpus before adopting). **If unsure, leave `CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001` pattern untouched in rev-002** and only add the insurance classifier; the spec below marks this optional.\n\n---\n\n## (C) NEW CLASSIFIERS\n\n### C1. `CLS-PII-USERNAME-001` \u2014 system account username\n\n**Precision problem with the generic pattern:** a naive `(?<![A-Za-z0-9._%+\\-])[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9._\\-]{{2,31}}(?![A-Za-z0-9.@])` **over-matches ordinary words, email local-parts and URL path segments** \u2014 measured false positives on the sentence *\"\u2026contact marcus.vance@example.com and see https://portal.example.com/mavance_admin and administrator\"*.\n\n**Context-anchored pattern that justifies \u22650.85 (validated).** Note this is a **capture-group** classifier: the emitted span is **group 1**, not group 0 (group 0 includes the `Account:` label):\n```json\n{{\n  \"classifier_id\": \"CLS-PII-USERNAME-001\",\n  \"category\": \"PII.IDENTIFIER.USERNAME\",\n  \"type\": \"regex\",\n  \"pattern\": \"(?:\\\\b(?:Account Name|Username|Account|Login|User)[ \\\\t]*:[ \\\\t]*)([a-z][a-z0-9._\\\\-]{{2,31}})(?![A-Za-z0-9.@\\\\-])\",\n  \"span_group\": 1,\n  \"confidence\": 0.86,\n  \"confidence_threshold\": 0.85,\n  \"priority\": 3,\n  \"mask_token\": \"[USERNAME]\",\n  \"validators\": [\n    {{ \"id\": \"not_email_localpart\", \"type\": \"negative_lookahead_guard\", \"spec\": \"reject if followed by '@' or if preceded by an email/URL token boundary\" }},\n    {{ \"id\": \"label_anchor_required\", \"type\": \"context_anchor\", \"spec\": \"account|username|login|user label with colon\" }}\n  ]\n}}\n```\nMeasured behaviour:\n\n| Input | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `Account: mavance_admin assigned; contact marcus.vance@example.com and see https://portal.example.com/mavance_admin and administrator` | **only** `mavance_admin`, group-1 span `(9,22)`; email, URL path and `administrator` **not** matched |\n| `Username: m.vance` | `m.vance` `(10,17)` |\n| `mavance_admin` (no label) | **no match** \u2014 proves context anchoring |\n| `user marcus.vance@example.com` | **no match** |\n| `Account mavance_admin` (no colon) | **no match** |\n\nIn the document's own text the same construct yields **`mavance_admin` at `[83,96]`** (the synthetic probe string yields 9\u201322 purely because of a shorter prefix).\n\n**Floor question, resolved:** (i) rev-001 has no global floor, so no *technical* exception is needed; (ii) the proposed **0.86 / threshold 0.85 is justified by the label anchoring** (label + colon is a mandatory, non-optional lookbehind, which is what makes the difference between ~0.75 naive precision and \u22650.85); (iii) **Admin decision D-3:** either accept 0.86/0.85 as specified, **or** if Admin elects to codify a *global PII floor = 0.85* as a new schema field, this classifier already complies. **No 0.75 variant is proposed.**\n**Implementation constraint:** Python `re` requires fixed-width look-behind, and `(?:Account|Username|User)` is variable width \u2014 **the consuming-prefix + `span_group: 1` form above is mandatory**; a `(?<=\u2026)` lookbehind form raises `error: look-behind requires fixed-width pattern` (observed).\n\n### C2. `CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001` \u2014 health insurance member identifier\n```json\n{{\n  \"classifier_id\": \"CLS-PHI-INSURANCE-MEMBER-ID-001\",\n  \"category\": \"PHI.MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER.HEALTH_INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID\",\n  \"type\": \"regex\",\n  \"pattern\": \"\\\\b[A-Z]{{2}}-\\\\d{{9}}-[A-Z]\\\\b\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.93,\n  \"confidence_threshold\": 0.90,\n  \"priority\": 2,\n  \"mask_token\": \"[INSURANCE_MEMBER_ID]\",\n  \"validators\": [\n    {{ \"id\": \"issuer_prefix_allowlist\", \"type\": \"dictionary_and_heuristic\",\n      \"spec\": \"2-char alpha payer/plan prefix (HI, BC, AH, UN, \u2026); Admin to confirm the closed list\" }},\n    {{ \"id\": \"segment_shape\", \"type\": \"heuristic\", \"spec\": \"exactly 9 numeric digits then one check alpha\" }}\n  ]\n}}\n```\nMeasured behaviour: `Member ID: HI-902849102-B on file` \u2192 match **`(11,25)`** = `HI-902849102-B`, length **14** \u2014 i.e. **`[403,417]` in the document**, exactly as required. `AB-123456789-X` \u2192 match. `not an id HI-90284-B` \u2192 no match.\n\n**Coexistence with `CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001`:**\n- **Priority:** both `priority: 2`. This is safe **by construction** because the prefix alphabets are **disjoint** (`HI` vs `MC|MEM|PAT|REC`), so the two patterns cannot overlap on the same character range.\n- **Overlap-resolution expectation: zero collisions on the current corpus** (expected \u2014 must be asserted by test, not assumed).\n- **If a future revision breaks disjointness**, the global resolver (see \u00a7H, which rev-002 must define because rev-001 has no `match_strategy`) decides: start offset ascending \u2192 longest match descending \u2192 priority ascending \u2192 confidence descending \u2192 keep highest-ranked non-overlapping span. Under that rule a 14-char `HI-\u2026` span